&lt;p&gt;Americans now view the Democratic Party as better equipped to manage the U.S. economy than the Republicans for the first time in nearly a decade, according to a Reuters/Ipsos poll that also found President Donald Trump's approval rating slipping to 35%.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The survey, conducted from Wednesday through Monday, suggests that concerns over the economy, including rising energy prices linked to the ongoing Iran war, could weigh heavily on Republican prospects in the November midterm elections, which will decide control of Congress for the next two years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The findings point to growing economic anxiety among voters as the conflict with Iran continues, with soaring fuel costs emerging as a key issue influencing public opinion.&lt;/p&gt;
